WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.330
I started writing a song
a day when I was 26,

00:03.760 --> 00:06.650
now I'm in my 40s and I'm still going.

00:06.760 --> 00:09.370
I've kept up Song A Day
through getting married,

00:09.380 --> 00:11.920
losing loved ones, the
birth of two children,

00:11.920 --> 00:13.450
and the adoption of a third.

00:13.540 --> 00:15.880
Song A Day has continued
through busy days,

00:15.880 --> 00:17.920
boring days, sick days, COVID days,

00:17.920 --> 00:19.830
and even hospital stays.

00:20.740 --> 00:22.760
The songs are not all great.

00:22.760 --> 00:25.700
In fact, in my opinion,
many of them are not.

00:25.700 --> 00:28.150
But of the many things I've learned,

00:28.180 --> 00:33.900
one important one is it is not up to
me to decide the value of the things

00:33.900 --> 00:38.280
I make. A song that I tossed off in
a moment between cooking dinner and

00:38.280 --> 00:42.040
putting the kids to bed will turn out
to be someone's favorite that I've

00:42.040 --> 00:44.660
ever done. And this
hasn't happened just once.

00:44.660 --> 00:46.690
It's like a regular occurrence.

00:47.040 --> 00:50.680
People like to talk about the act
of being consistent in the way they

00:50.680 --> 00:53.070
create and share quote-unquote content.

00:53.680 --> 00:57.360
But I found that there's the
consistency in content and there's

00:57.360 --> 00:59.410
consistency in your practice.

00:59.980 --> 01:03.750
Consistent content is what the
algorithm craves and demands.

01:04.020 --> 01:06.750
It's choosing a niche and
sticking within those confines.

01:06.860 --> 01:10.500
If you're writing a song a day, it
means using the same instrument every

01:10.500 --> 01:12.690
day, framing your video the same way,

01:12.720 --> 01:16.320
writing songs that are more or less
in the same genre on topics that don't

01:16.320 --> 01:17.510
vary too widely.

01:17.800 --> 01:21.230
But that kind of
consistency just isn't me.

01:21.280 --> 01:23.860
The world of recording is so vast,

01:23.860 --> 01:27.940
the world of creating a video is so
enormous that I long ago made the

01:27.940 --> 01:31.980
decision to sacrifice what the algorithm
wants for what I want to be free

01:31.980 --> 01:36.240
to make a song about whatever topic
using whatever instrumentation and any

01:36.240 --> 01:38.490
type of video techniques
that interests me.

01:38.660 --> 01:40.700
This has meant that
when a song goes viral,

01:40.700 --> 01:43.420
most people don't stick
around or more accurately,

01:43.420 --> 01:47.090
the algorithm learns to shuffle
them off in another direction.

01:47.160 --> 01:52.010
Because one day I'll produce a track
that goes “Baby Yoda, baby baby Yoda.”

01:52.140 --> 01:55.080
Then the next day improvise a
song on the electric guitar about

01:55.080 --> 01:58.240
impeachment hearings, then make a
track produced around a song I wrote

01:58.240 --> 02:00.060
called “I Won't Make That Mistake Again”,

02:00.060 --> 02:02.890
and then a song where I'm sitting
under my desk playing the bass.

02:02.900 --> 02:05.170
The baby Yoda song got 9 million views.

02:05.440 --> 02:08.290
The subsequent ones got
less than 2000 combined.

02:08.400 --> 02:11.600
I know that if I followed the
rules of consistent content,

02:11.600 --> 02:13.200
I would have a much larger audience.

02:13.200 --> 02:16.780
But lately, I've been thinking that
I also might not have done the best

02:16.780 --> 02:19.890
job of framing what Song A Day is.

02:19.980 --> 02:23.810
You shouldn't arrive to Song A Day
thinking you like every song.

02:23.880 --> 02:27.600
Some days are bangers, and
some days are just Tuesday.

02:27.600 --> 02:31.000
Or that because you heard one acoustic
ballad about video games that you

02:31.000 --> 02:33.780
can expect to hear something
like that every single day.

02:33.780 --> 02:38.260
What you should expect is just me
interpreting through songs my life and

02:38.260 --> 02:44.000
the world as I experience it, and
all its beauty and injustice and hope

02:44.000 --> 02:45.170
and ugliness.

02:46.340 --> 02:48.090
If that sounds interesting to you,

02:48.620 --> 02:50.390
welcome to Song A Day. 